# Pairs with FenceEventuallyReleased. The fence's lease lapses only while its move
# is live - expiry is something the coordinator notices, not a property of the
# record - so a fence whose coordinator has been lost is never released and the
# source refuses appends for ever. The base lease lapses unconditionally.
# DEADLOCK: off is required: once appends are refused for ever the stream reaches
# a state with no successor, which TLC reports as a deadlock before it checks the
# liveness property this mutation targets.
MODULE: FenceEventuallyReleasedOrphanedLeaseNeverLapses
TARGET: FenceEventuallyReleased
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a lost coordinator's fence never lapses, so it is never released
PERTURBS: LeaseLapse
DEADLOCK: off

--- FIND
    /\ dfence # NoMove
    /\ ~lapsed
    /\ lapsed' = TRUE
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: only a live move's lease can lapse.
    /\ dfence # NoMove
    /\ ~lapsed
    /\ move[dfence] \in {"fenced", "copied"}
    /\ lapsed' = TRUE
--- END
